 # Current limitations
 
+- The batch functions work on a material data manager, whose arrays are
+  stored point by point. `TFEL` supports other layouts (component by
+  component, arbitrary strides), better suited to coalesced accesses on
+  GPUs: they are not exposed yet. The material properties are evaluated
+  on contiguous or uniform values.
+- `update` and `revert` copy the states on the host.
+- `MaterialFunctionManager` builds its material data manager on the host.
 - The optional arrays giving the status and the time step scaling factor
   of each point are not exposed.
 - The `C`, `Fortran` and `Python` bindings do not expose the new
